    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), our premier play against Canning. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor and a 9% boost from the favorable SP skill, making him the highest-ceiling asset in the group. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-utility of our outfield; **Kyle Tucker** (75.85) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) both capitalize on strong matchups, with **Jackson Merrill** receiving an additional efficiency bump due to the pitcher's slow delivery, which creates a prime environment for him to exploit the stolen base category\u2014our most critical scarcity target. **Andy Pages** (70.46) also draws a favorable setup against Kay, utilizing a 19% SP skill advantage to secure his spot as a high-floor producer.\n\nMid-tier decisions are largely dictated by platoon advantages and lineup positioning. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.44) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.44) provide reliable output, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefiting from a significant 14% platoon edge against Miller. The most intriguing bench decision was **Josh Jung** (53.35), who performed admirably but ultimately fell short of the starting threshold due to a tougher matchup against Gray. **Josh Jung** remains our top depth piece should any last-minute lineup shuffles occur. Meanwhile, **Dominic Smith** (40.45) barely clears our floor; while he is currently active, he remains a candidate for mid-game substitution if he struggles early against McLean\u2019s elite 3.33 xERA. We are monitoring the weather closely, though the current projections suggest no major atmospheric volatility that would shift these efficiency scores further.",
